Finally gave up and took by smartest bot into some key operational Slack channels.  Works great until we actually need him to do work.  I have dozens of keys, credentials, etc.. with this bot (who was already a shared bot with my team).  All that is wasted, he cant share ANYTHING with himself.  Apparently he got a new computer for the Slack connection and lost access to all previous assets.   Why???   Quit bragging about the power of team bots when they are NOT the SAME BOT.  They are silo'd copies but they cannot communicate and exchange data from my experience, and I think it is DUMB that we have had to burn a ton of tokens basically littering my Google Drive with "exchange logs" between my Grok Bot app bots and my Slack integrated bots...  

FIX THIS PLEASE.  If a team bot gets knowledge, credentials, etc. inside the app, that same team bot should have that knowledge and assets in Slack.

